{% extends "base.jinja" %}
{% block title %}
  {{ super() }} | {{ ftl_get_message("handoff-done-title") }}
{% endblock title %}
{% block content %}
  {# Where a browser is left after signing in on an app's behalf
     (src/handoff.rs), once the person here has said it was they who asked
     (identity_handoff_confirm.jinja). Nothing was signed in here: this
     window carried what the provider said back to the app, which is going
     on by itself.

     So the one thing left is to put the app back in front, which it cannot
     do for itself from here -- a tab the browser opened is not one a script
     may close. `oeee-cafe://handoff/done?code=<code>` is what does it, and
     it carries the one thing the app needs from this window: the code its
     claim has to bring, 64 lowercase hex characters, which the app hands
     the page as window.oeeeApp.signIn.resume(code) (app_sign_in.jinja).
     The code reaches only an app on this device, which is the point: a
     handoff somebody else started, and sent this browser the link to, is
     never theirs to claim. The apps load nothing from the URL
     (AndroidManifest.xml in oeee-cafe-android, handoff.rs in
     oeee-cafe-desktop, the callback scheme of ASWebAuthenticationSession in
     oeee-cafe-apple). Reached without a code -- /auth/handoff/done by
     itself -- the URL carries none.

     The link is here to be pressed as well as followed by itself. A browser
     may refuse to leave for another application without somebody asking it
     to, and whoever reached this page in an ordinary browser -- with no app
     waiting -- has something to read instead of an error. #}
  {% set back = "oeee-cafe://handoff/done" ~ ("?code=" ~ code if code else "") %}
  <div class="auth-page">
    <div class="ds-card auth-card">
      <h1 class="auth-title">{{ ftl_get_message("handoff-done-title") }}</h1>
      <p class="auth-lede">{{ ftl_get_message("handoff-done-body") }}</p>
      <a class="ds-button ds-button-primary auth-submit"
         href="oeee-cafe://handoff/done{% if code %}?code={{ code }}{% endif %}">{{ ftl_get_message("handoff-done-return") }}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script>if (window.oeeeChrome) window.oeeeChrome.handoffDone({{ back|tojson }});</script>
{% endblock content %}
